================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY COPYRIGHT NOTICE & LICENSING TERMS
================================================================================

This dataset contains adapted and translated material derived from third-party clinical guidelines, government health resources, and scientific publications. The copyright and licensing status of each underlying source remains governed by its respective original license:

1. Directorate General of Health Services (DGHS), Bangladesh:
   - National Guideline on Diabetes Mellitus (2023) and National Protocol for Management of Diabetes and Hypertension (2018–19).
   - Reuse remains subject to the applicable terms of the original source.

2. Diabetes Association of Bangladesh (BADAS):
   - BADAS Guideline (2019) and Guideline for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus in Bangladesh (2003).
   - Reuse remains subject to the applicable terms of the original source.

3. World Health Organization (WHO):
   - WHO Guideline on Carbohydrate Intake (2023), governed by CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO.
   - Non-commercial sharing, adaptation, and redistribution are permitted with attribution and ShareAlike.
   - Any translation is unofficial and does not imply WHO endorsement.

4. National Health Service (NHS), UK:
   - NHS starchy foods and carbohydrates guidelines, licensed under Open Government Licence (OGL) v3.0.
   - Copying and adaptation are permitted subject to NHS terms, attribution, and non-endorsement conditions.

5. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), USA:
   - CDC health material (Smoking and Diabetes, Road to Health Toolkit, Diabetes Plate Method).
   - Mostly public domain, subject to CDC attribution and non-endorsement requirements.

6. National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (NIDDK, NIH), USA:
   - NIDDK educational resources (Healthy Living with Diabetes).
   - Copyright-free website content reproducible with attribution, subject to stated NIDDK conditions.

7. Open Access Scientific Literature (CC BY 4.0):
   - Meng et al. (2019) (Effects and Mechanisms of Tea for the Prevention and Management of Diabetes Mellitus and Diabetic Complications).
   - Amoah et al. (2025) (Glycaemic and satiety responses associated with the consumption of parboiled and braised rice).
   - Free reuse, adaptation, translation, and redistribution permitted under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International.

The CC BY-NC 4.0 license applied to the authors' original contributions does not override, replace, or expand the rights granted by any third-party source license.

================================================================================
MEDICAL DISCLAIMER
================================================================================

This dataset is compiled strictly for computational linguistics, Natural Language Processing (NLP), and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) research purposes. It is NOT intended to be used as direct medical advice, clinical decision support, or a replacement for professional healthcare consultation.